    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Nasim Nunez** anchoring the production expectations at a 62.09 efficiency score. While he hits ninth, the matchup against Feltner (5.10 xERA) is a primary driver; the combination of a favorable park adjustment and his elite sprint speed makes him our highest-ceiling play for steals in a 5x5 format. **Sam Antonacci** follows closely with a 59.34 score, benefiting significantly from his leadoff spot against Kumar Rocker. While Rocker\u2019s xERA is middling, **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s ability to leverage his dynamic platoon advantage and favorable lineup placement provides the most reliable floor among our starting middle infielders today.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision centered on the utility spot, where **Miguel Vargas** (54.63) narrowly edged out internal projections for the remaining depth pieces like **Andy Pages** and **Coby Mayo**. **Miguel Vargas** earns the nod due to a strong 0.389 xwOBA and an advantageous position in the heart of the order, even though the matchup against Rocker is less exploitable than the one **Nasim Nunez** faces. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (51.54) remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against Braxton Ashcraft; his score is buoyed by a dynamic platoon adjustment, but he remains a high-variance play given the pitcher\u2019s ability to suppress contact. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Tommy White**, whose 55.05 projection is contingent on the pending lineup confirmation; should he drop out of the #5 spot, his efficiency score will likely dip below the optimal threshold. As we manage our game caps, the bench remains heavy with heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**, all of whom are unavailable today due to team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** also sidelined, the pressure is on **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** to catalyze our counting stats, as the current depth chart requires a disciplined approach to avoid wasting cap space on marginal, low-ceiling performers like **Dominic Smith** or **Wade Meckler** in the face of today\u2019s matchups.",
